# Keep LF on checkout for everything that gets executed or byte-compared:
# bash scripts (CI and local runs), and the golden .txt files the tests diff.
* text=auto

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.go   text eol=lf
*.c    text eol=lf
*.asm  text eol=lf
# LLVM/GAS assembly: LF is not cosmetic here. A CRLF checkout leaves a stray \r
# at the end of every line, which the AT&T front end then reads as part of the
# last operand -- turning `movq %rax, %rcx` into a call through a register
# called `rcx\r`. The .s files under goa/testdata/att are byte-compared
# against what LLVM emits, so they have to survive checkout unchanged.
*.s    text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
